From: xnulinux <xnulinux@local>
Subject: [PATCH] venus: create graphics and compute pipelines synchronously on Darwin

When the Venus host renderer runs on MoltenVK (macOS), SPIRV-Cross / Metal
shader compilation can reject a pipeline with VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED
(-3). With Mesa Venus's default async pipeline creation on the primary ring,
vn_Create{Graphics,Compute}Pipelines returns VK_SUCCESS immediately with an
unregistered client handle, causing callers (such as metal2vulkan's
multi_variable_dynamic_creates self-check) to miss the failure and causing
subsequent vkDestroyPipeline/vkCmdBindPipeline calls to hit a fatal CS error
on unhardened virglrenderer.

Force synchronous pipeline creation (want_sync = true) under #ifdef __APPLE__.
Note that #ifdef __APPLE__ checks that the guest is Darwin (not that the host
renderer is MoltenVK); this Darwin build of Venus exclusively serves hosted
macOS whose host renderer is MoltenVK, so both always hold together here and
the guest always receives the real VkResult from the host driver and takes its
fallback path cleanly.

---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_pipeline.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_pipeline.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_pipeline.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_pipeline.c
@@ -1683,7 +1683,11 @@ vn_CreateGraphicsPipelines(VkDevice device,
    struct vn_device *dev = vn_device_from_handle(device);
    const VkAllocationCallbacks *alloc =
       pAllocator ? pAllocator : &dev->base.vk.alloc;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+   bool want_sync = true;
+#else
    bool want_sync = false;
+#endif
    VkResult result;
 
    /* silence -Wmaybe-uninitialized false alarm on release build with gcc */
@@ -1775,7 +1779,11 @@ vn_CreateComputePipelines(VkDevice device,
    struct vn_device *dev = vn_device_from_handle(device);
    const VkAllocationCallbacks *alloc =
       pAllocator ? pAllocator : &dev->base.vk.alloc;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+   bool want_sync = true;
+#else
    bool want_sync = false;
+#endif
    VkResult result;
 
    memset(pPipelines, 0, sizeof(*pPipelines) * createInfoCount);
